 # Working notes: 6b266391d6b7
 
-Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
-Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+## Defect
+
+The generator correctly kept five executable wrong rules in
+`LESSON_COMPETITORS`, but also aliased them into `CANONICAL_SHORTCUTS`. That
+second declaration was false: erase-only, first-marker-only, solid-2×2, and
+monochrome stamping each fail all five labeled canonical pairs; fixed-lower-L
+fails three of five. The native semantic gate therefore rejected the source.
+
+## Repair
+
+Added an allowed regression at
+`tests/test_canonical_shortcut_contract.py` requiring every declared canonical
+shortcut to fit every labeled canonical pair. With the old alias restored, this
+test failed first on `erase_markers_only`; after the repair it passes. The source
+change is deliberately one declaration: the five rivals remain executable
+`SEMANTIC_RIVALS` and `LESSON_COMPETITORS`, while `CANONICAL_SHORTCUTS` is now an
+empty typed mapping. No lesson-generation or canonical-label behavior changed.
+
+The baseline task-root `test_generator_6b266391d6b7.py` is a frozen fixture and
+was restored byte-for-byte. It was not patched to hide its portability defect.
+
+## Verification
+
+- Focused regression red replay: one expected failure on
+  `erase_markers_only`.
+- Focused regression green replay: 1 passed.
+- Native semantic gate: passed.
+- Semantic census: 600/600 strict draws across easy, medium, and hard; zero
+  crashes; declared lesson witnesses and rival separation retained.
